  "headline": "Refund limits now include a shipping share that is split over all shipped lines, which can over- or under-refund shipping, and the API status code for rejected amounts changed from 400 to 422.",
  "reasons": [
    {
      "effect": "raises",
      "severity": "medium",
      "title": "Shipping share rounding and uneven split",
      "because": "allocateShipping divides shippingTotal by the number of shipped lines with Math.round and multiplies by the number of picked lines. When the cents do not divide evenly, the shares can add up to more or less than the shipping paid. Picking every shipped line of three, for example, returns 3 x round(cents/3), which can differ from the total.",
      "why": "Refund limits for partly shipped orders can be off by a cent or more, and the split ignores line value.",
      "test": {
        "status": "partial",
        "note": "Tests cover a two-line split and a single line, but not an uneven division such as three lines.",
